# state: any   (golden 9153c63300da, the same as gta-3.route)
# Grand Theft Auto III (5454000E): a DRIVING route (lane.gta3drive1017, #433).
# NOT PROVEN until a run's frames show the car moving: frames minutes apart at
# different places, radar turning. gta-3.route is the on-foot measurement and
# stays as it is.
#
# Boot: copied verbatim from gta-3.route up to its `waitfor fist-hud` (see
# that file's header for why there is no START).
#
# Entry gate: the scene itself, Claude on foot beside the Kuruma on the
# bridge ramp (refs/gta-3-drive/at-kuruma.png, the car and the wall behind
# it, cut from 1-1792280173-...-1364097 164333-pregameplay.png at
# 830,440,450,220). Three of five runs reach exactly this frame by
# `pregameplay` (1364097, 1364296, and the Playable run
# 1-1791792686-lane.local-32437) and stand in it until input moves them
# (1364097: unchanged from 16:43:33 to 16:50:00). tools/route_gate.py: 0.00,
# 0.25, 0.37-0.67 on those frames; 19.87 and up on the 31 others (cutscenes,
# the in-car frames, the drives). Threshold 10.
#
# Two gates before this one failed:
# - fist-hud (gta-3.route's) matched at once in both pilots
#   (1-1792275531-...-343857, 1-1792275540-...-346093), whose A-train ended
#   with Claude already in a car in Red Light District / Chinatown at a 05:xx
#   clock (153645-pregameplay.png, 154630-pregameplay.png); the Y press
#   there exited the car. The weapon icon is up on every in-game screen.
# - the tutorial box "Enter or exit a vehicle: Y" (enter-help.png) never
#   showed after `pregameplay` in either run of the first drive pair: it is
#   up only in the first seconds of the mission, which the A-train covers.
#   Both runs timed out on it, standing beside the car.
# A run whose A-train ends anywhere else times out here and is void.
#
# Entry: press Y until the scene changes (press-until's reference is the
# state before the press works). The game takes the nearest upright car
# within 10 units (re3 CPlayerInfo::FindClosestCarSectorList,
# `dist <= 10.0f`), so one Y walks Claude to the door and in, and the camera
# swings behind the car; up to 3 presses 5 s apart cover a press the host's
# adb drops (both pilots logged vsock accept timeouts). The 6 s after it
# covers the camera swing and the "Accelerate" box. 8-Ball is already in the
# passenger seat by then: 1-1792282254-...-1563459's onfoot frame (clock
# 05:12) shows him in it before the Y press.
#
# Warm-up, before `mark gameplay`: the same driving as the scored loop's laps for
# ~65 s (five laps, no back-up) with a frame every ~2-3 s. In 1563459 the gate and the entry worked
# (matched at 0 s, in after one Y), but the mission restarted within ~30 s of
# the throttle (clock 05:25 in the car at 17:14:12, 04:18 on foot beside the
# Kuruma at 17:14:46), and Claude stayed on foot for the rest of the run. No
# frame covered those 30 s. These do, and they are outside the scored window,
# so their screencaps cost the measurement nothing. `mark gameplay` comes
# after them, so the scored window starts in a car that has been moving.
#
# Driving: RT accelerates (pad.sh: the triggers are not swapped; 0..32767),
# LT brakes and reverses, LX steers (-32767..32767; both Nova and Thor cache
# the same ranges). Equal left and right pulses hold the heading on average.
# Every third lap brakes straight, then backs up with the wheel turned, so a
# wall or a lamp post cannot hold the car. Never Y after the entry (it would
# exit), never START or BACK.
#
# Gentle on purpose. 1-1792283158-...-1853100 drove full throttle with 0.6 s
# full-lock pulses: up the ramp, then on the first left pulse the Kuruma rode
# the right-hand barrier onto its roof (172943-warm.png, clock 05:51), and
# the mission failed, "You flipped your wheels!" (172945). The mission
# restarts with Claude on foot beside the car, and a route has no
# conditionals to get him back in. So: RT 22000 (about two thirds), LX
# +-12000 (about a third of lock) for 0.8 s, and the back-up brakes with the
# wheel straight for 1 s before it turns (full lock in reverse is slow).
#
wait 55
repeat 4 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot introskip
repeat 12 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot pregameplay
waitfor at-kuruma 240 830,440,450,220 10
shot onfoot
press-until Y at-kuruma 3 5 830,440,450,220 10
wait 6
shot incar
repeat 5 {
    axis RT 22000
    wait 2
    shot warm
    wait 2
    shot warm
    axis LX -12000
    wait 0.8
    axis LX mid
    wait 1.5
    shot warm
    wait 1.5
    shot warm
    axis LX 12000
    wait 0.8
    axis LX mid
    wait 2
    shot warm
}
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    repeat 3 {
        axis RT 22000
        wait 4
        axis LX -12000
        wait 0.8
        axis LX mid
        wait 3
        axis LX 12000
        wait 0.8
        axis LX mid
        wait 2
    }
    shot drive
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    wait 1
    axis LX max
    wait 2
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
}
